   Let’s normalize EHVI relative to Option 0 (pure exploitation) to see marginal losses:

   \[
   \text{EHVI}_\text{rel}(\text{opt }i) = \frac{\text{EHVI}_i}{0.4012}
   \]
   - Opt 0: 1.000  
   - Opt 1: 0.3430 / 0.4012 ≈ 0.855  
   - Opt 2: 0.3072 / 0.4012 ≈ 0.766  
