6. **Balancing EHVI vs entropy under current conditions**  
   We want to trade exploitation (EHVI) against exploration (entropy). Formally, if we imagine a simple scalarized utility  
   \[
   U_i = \alpha \cdot \text{EHVI}_i + \beta \cdot \text{Entropy}_i,
   \]
   then for any nonnegative \((\alpha, \beta)\) with \(\alpha > 0\), Option 0 is dominant because:  
   - It has **maximum EHVI**, and  
   - It also has **maximum entropy** among all options.  

   That implies Option 0 is Pareto-dominant in the (EHVI, Entropy) plane: no other option provides more entropy without sacrificing more EHVI, and none provides more EHVI with more entropy. Given our phase (not extremely early, not on last iteration), this is an ideal situation—no need to accept reduced EHVI just to gain information.

