     - \(n_{\text{opt}}\) = expected fraction of future points spent on optimization,
     - \(n_{\text{expl}}\) = expected fraction on exploration,
     then \(n_{\text{opt}} + n_{\text{expl}} = 1\).  
   - A heavy-exploit policy like Option 1 (4 opt + 1 expl) corresponds to:
