     - Score each option by \( S_i = \alpha \tilde{E}_i + (1-\alpha) \tilde{H}_i \) with \(\alpha\) tilted toward 1 when trend is positive and runway is long.  
     - Here, the unnormalized data already show Option 0 as the unique maximizer on both axes ⇒ it maximizes any such linear scalarization for \(0 < \alpha < 1\).

