     - Option 2: Slightly more exploration, but ~10% EHVI drop; given the medium runway and strong recent best point, this is more exploratory than necessary at this stage.

8. **Quantitative Utility Approximation per Iteration**  
   - If we define a simple scalar utility as a weighted sum of normalized EHVI and Entropy:
     \[
     U(\text{option}) = \alpha \cdot \frac{\text{EHVI}}{\text{EHVI}_\text{max}} + \beta \cdot \frac{\text{Entropy}}{\text{Entropy}_\text{max}}
     \]
     where \(\text{EHVI}_\text{max}=0.8038\), \(\text{Entropy}_\text{max}=0.07\).  
   - With weights \(\alpha=0.7\) (prioritizing exploitation given runway) and \(\beta=0.3\):
     - Option 0:  
