   - The ratio objective \(R = K/|\text{CTE}|\) is extremely sensitive when \(|\text{CTE}|\) is small: small improvements in \(|\text{CTE}|\) (further reduction in magnitude) near zero can cause *nonlinear* boosts in \(R\).  
   - Around the current best (with CTE ≈ −0.012), localized exploitation is particularly valuable: the gradient of \(R\) w.r.t. CTE is on the order of
     \[
     \frac{\partial R}{\partial |\text{CTE}|} \approx -\frac{K}{|\text{CTE}|^2}
     \]
