     - Opt 3: EHVI 0.2556, Entropy 0.25  
     - Opt 4: EHVI 0.1873, Entropy 0.12  
     - Opt 5: EHVI 0.1902, Entropy 0.19  

   - Option 3 has **near-best EHVI** (0.2556 vs 0.2756, only ~7.3% below the maximum) but **highest entropy** (0.25, ~39% higher than 0.18 and >2× that of 0.12).  
   - Formally, define a simple utility that linearly weighs exploitation and exploration in this early–mid phase:  
     \[
     U = \alpha \cdot \text{EHVI} + \beta \cdot \text{Entropy}, \quad \alpha \approx \beta
     \]
     If we set α = β = 1 (equal early-phase weighting):
     - U₀ = 0.2756 + 0.18 = 0.4556  
