   We want a utility function reflecting trade-off between exploitation (EHVI) and exploration (entropy). A simple linearized surrogate:

   \[
   U_i(\alpha) = \text{EHVI}_i + \alpha \cdot H_i
   \]

   where \(\alpha\) is an implicit exchange rate between 1 unit of entropy and 1 unit of EHVI.

5. **Reasonable trade-off regime**  
   - We are not at the very beginning (80 points already), so pure exploration (Option 5) is too conservative.  
   - We are not at the very end of runway either (≈4 iterations left), so pure exploitation (Option 0) risks premature convergence around the current local optimum.  
