       - Runway is moderate (~4 iterations), not “short” in the sense of a last-iteration Hail Mary.  
   - Therefore, a near-pure exploitation option is consistent with the intended policy logic.

10. **Policy implication (dynamic strategy)**  
    - Early/mid campaign: mixed options (1–3) help shape a good global model.  
    - Late campaign + strong incumbent + improving trend: shift toward **max-EHVI, modest-entropy option**.  
    - Here, Option 0 has the highest EHVI and nearly maximal entropy among all options; it is the natural choice according to a dynamic policy:
      \[
      \text{Select } \arg\max_{\text{option}} \left[ \lambda \cdot \text{EHVI} + (1-\lambda) \cdot \text{Entropy} \right]
      \]
      with \(\lambda\) high (~0.8–0.9) in the late phase. Numerically, such a scoring function would rank Option 0 first for any \(\lambda \gtrsim 0.2\).

