   The *maximal* expected hypervolume improvement is obtained by Option 0:
   \[
     \max_i \text{EHVI}_i = 0.2930 = \text{EHVI}_0
   \]
   The next best, Option 2, is:
   \[
     \text{EHVI}_2 = 0.2632 \quad \Rightarrow \quad
     \frac{\text{EHVI}_0 - \text{EHVI}_2}{\text{EHVI}_0}
     \approx \frac{0.2930 - 0.2632}{0.2930} \approx 10.2\% \text{ lower}
   \]
   So Option 0 yields ~10% higher expected Pareto improvement than the best mixed explore–exploit alternative.

4. **Information gain (entropy) comparison**  
   Let \( H_i \) be the mutual information (entropy) metric for option \( i \):  
   - \( H_0 = 0.10 \)  
   - \( H_1 = 0.06 \)  
   - \( H_2 = 0.14 \)  
   - \( H_3 = 0.11 \)  
