   - \( H_5 = 0.23 \)

   Option 5 has the largest entropy (0.23), but its EHVI (0.2537) is notably worse than Option 0 (0.2930). The trade-off:

   - Relative gain in entropy of Option 5 vs 0:
     \[
       \Delta H = \frac{H_5 - H_0}{H_0} = \frac{0.23 - 0.10}{0.10} = 130\% \text{ higher}
     \]
   - Relative loss in EHVI:
     \[
       \Delta \text{EHVI} = \frac{\text{EHVI}_0 - \text{EHVI}_5}{\text{EHVI}_0}
       \approx \frac{0.2930 - 0.2537}{0.2930}
