     \]
     So 4 gives a bit more entropy, but at a large immediate cost in predicted performance improvement. With ~17 iterations left and accelerating gains, this much sacrifice in EHVI is premature; policy should transition to heavier exploration only when marginal EHVI stops improving or begins to plateau.

